        {
            "title": "東京11月CPI持穩，核心通膨略低於預期",
            "description": "<div class=\"atoms\" data-component=\"blocks\"><figure class=\"mb-module-gap\"><div class=\"mx-auto w-fit max-w-full\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"rounded-lg\" fetchpriority=\"high\" height=\"757\" src=\"https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/fb1ccccd93cf2be83e383e3c7da59001b7e00d33ce2f08c5516619d937d08406/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w1200%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fcontent-media.investing.com%2Fnews%2FLYNXMPECBL09K_M.jpg\" width=\"1200\"/></div></figure><p class=\"mb-module-gap break-words leading-[1.4] text-px20 lg:text-px18 lg:leading-[1.8] text-batcave\">Investing.com - 東京11月消費者通膨維持穩定，核心通膨雖略低於市場預期，但仍高於日本央行（BOJ）的目標水準。</p><p class=\"mb-module-gap break-words leading-[1.4] text-px20 lg:text-px18 lg:leading-[1.8] text-batcave\">政府數據於週五公布，東京核心消費者物價指數（剔除波動性較大的生鮮食品價格）11月按年上漲2.9%，略低於市場預期的3.0%，但高於上月的2.6%。</p><p class=\"mb-module-gap break-words leading-[1.4] text-px20 lg:text-px18 lg:leading-[1.8] text-batcave\">同時剔除生鮮食品及能源價格的核心讀數，11月從上月的2.6%降至2.5%。這一數據是日本央行衡量基礎通膨的重要指標，受到市場密切關注。</p><div class=\"bg-toast-background -mx-5 -mt-2 mb-3 pb-3 md:-mx-0 lg:mx-auto lg:w-[300px] lg:pb-0\"><div class=\"text-px14 text-gandalf py-1 text-center leading-5\">廣告</div><div class=\"mx-auto text-center min-w-[300px] min-h-[250px]\" id=\"sda-inbody-735d236f-e66a-3d49-bc33-1e019a4bd93d-1-iframe\"><div class=\"bg-dirty-seagull text-px12 text-dolphin mx-auto hidden items-center justify-center only:flex w-[300px] h-[250px]\">廣告</div></div></div><p class=\"mb-module-gap break-words leading-[1.4] text-px20 lg:text-px18 lg:leading-[1.8] text-batcave\">東京CPI整體數據11月按年上漲2.8%，高於上月的2.7%。</p><div class=\"recommendation-contents\"><div class=\"bg-marshmallow mb-2 h-[30px] w-[80px] rounded-lg\"></div><div class=\"no-scrollbar -mx-5 mb-5 flex overflow-hidden overflow-x-auto md:-mx-2 lg:mb-3.5\"><div class=\"bg-marshmallow mr-2 ml-5 h-[94px] w-[calc(85%-28px)] flex-shrink-0 rounded-lg md:ml-2 md:w-[calc(85%-16px)] lg:w-[300px]\"></div><div class=\"bg-marshmallow mx-2 h-[94px] w-[85%] flex-shrink-0 rounded-lg lg:w-[300px]\"></div><div class=\"bg-marshmallow hidden h-[94px] w-[300px] flex-shrink-0 rounded-lg lg:block\"></div></div></div><p class=\"mb-module-gap break-words leading-[1.4] text-px20 lg:text-px18 lg:leading-[1.8] text-batcave\">週五公布的數據顯示，核心通膨仍遠高於日本央行2%的目標，這一趨勢可能促使央行在未來數月內進一步加息。</p><p class=\"mb-module-gap break-words leading-[1.4] text-px20 lg:text-px18 lg:leading-[1.8] text-batcave\">日本央行於10月實際上宣告在對抗通縮的戰役中取得勝利，為進一步收緊貨幣政策打開了大門。</p><p class=\"mb-module-gap break-words leading-[1.4] text-px20 lg:text-px18 lg:leading-[1.8] text-batcave\">日本通膨今年持續攀升，主要受到日圓疲軟、國內消費穩健以及能源價格上漲等因素支撐。</p><p class=\"mb-module-gap break-words leading-[1.4] text-px20 lg:text-px18 lg:leading-[1.8] text-batcave\">儘管政府對燃料及公用事業的補貼有助於抑制消費者通膨的升幅，但生產者通膨今年大幅上揚，市場普遍預期企業將把成本轉嫁給消費者。</p><p class=\"mb-module-gap break-words leading-[1.4] text-px20 lg:text-px18 lg:leading-[1.8] text-batcave\"><em>此文章由人工智能協助翻譯。更多資訊，請參閱我們的使用條款。</em></p></div>",
